#{
  // print control on user content (plan P3-14): a lemma keeps with the block
  // after it; the proof keeps together
  $.set({role: 'lemma'}, {keep: 'with-next'})
  $.set({role: 'proof'}, {keep: 'together'})
}

= Keeps

Filler paragraph one fills most of the first sheet with ordinary running text so that the lemma comes close to the bottom edge of the sheet.

#!lemma
A lemma that fits at the foot of the sheet.
#lemma!

#!proof
Its proof, three lines long, which the lemma keeps with: neither is left alone at a sheet's foot, and the proof itself is not cut.
#proof!

After the proof.
